From 4003fae04cf9a2dfb0fa8ce4bc6cb60a95c23a28 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Mike Kinney <mike.kinney@gmail.com>
Date: Fri, 20 Nov 2026 14:11:25 -0800
Subject: [PATCH] fix(import): refuse a STEP item with no unit context in a
 degree file

The STEP reader gives a solid item that no representation lists the
default units, so it reads the angles of that item in radians. In a file
that states a plane angle unit in degrees, the item had wrong geometry
and the import gave no warning.

The model read now refuses such an item by name when a context of the
file states a plane angle unit that is not the radian. A built solid is
refused, and the unit reason replaces the message of an item that failed
to read. A file that states only the radian keeps the item.

Fixes #3079

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
